e think politics is playing a  role but it's hard for me to not see  what's happening in Michigan seeing the  outrage and the slow roll out and wonder  if the Democratic governor like the  Democratic governor of Maine and the  Democratic governor of California are  creating outrage because the citizens  are seeing the  eat faster pace with the rollout and I  just hope the Democratic governors  aren't going I'm in no rush to turn this  economy around for this president do you  fear that or am I am i overthinking it  look I think these governors are trying  to make the best decisions they can but  ultimately they have to remember that  they have an obligation to the people of  their state to allow them to provide for  their families and if everyone else and  they get to a place where they can  safely do that they have one obligation  to at some point allow that to take  place  I think we need to provide the support  the resources and again I think the  president has done exactly the right  thing in providing that flexibility  providing financial resources for states  and in terms of supplies so that they  can do that and if yes to continue to do  that and hopefully the governor's will  make the right decision to do what's  best for the people in their communities  both protecting their health and  protecting their economies because at  the end of the day those people are  going to be voted for as well they'll  either get to keep their jobs or not  because they did the right thing by the  people in those communities that's right  so Sara we've all had to find ways to  talk to our children about this  depending on their age we give them  specifics my daughter's 4 so she doesn't  really understand this but I know you  how old are your kids I have an 8 year  old a six year old and a four year old  okay so the president was asked about it  how he's telling his son how he's  talking to his son about it and and his  grandkids listen to this I sat down with  my son I sat down with my grandchildren  I said a terrible thing that's happened  it's a thing that we've never  experienced but I said something's  happened but we're going to be strong  and we're gonna get out of it and our  country is going to be bigger and better  and stronger than ever before how did  you talk to your children Sara much in  the same way you know I think the most  important thing we can do is be honest  with our kids and be transparent my kids  are young so it's hard for them to  process everything that's going on they  don't understand why they can't go to  school and why they can't play with  their friend  every day but at the same time we've  tried to really focus on some of the  positive things that we still live in  the greatest country on the face of the  planet we have a God who loves us and  ultimately this is all under his control  and we've got to spend a lot of time  together as a family we've been  homeschooling our kids that could be to  their detriment but it's been a learning  experience for all of us but at the end  of the day we've tried to be honest with  our kids it can be very difficult to  hear your four-year-old pray every night  that he hopes nobody gets killed in his  family from the virus but at the same  time we try to reinforce that again we  have a God that loves us and that we are  still in America in the most resilient  and tough country and we will come back  and we will come back stronger and we're  gonna do that together as a family and  as a country that's right we're in this  together sir what do you make of the  fact that over the last week or so the  president has stopped doing the nightly  five o'clock or 6 o'clock p.m. press  briefings where it might go half hour  might go two hours and instead does more  targeted events during the day like that  small business day it's first responders  day where he has guests into the White  House and then you had the big event  last night at the Lincoln Memorial is  that effective more effective and  getting the message out I saw that over  the last two weeks I think it was Gallup  says that the president's ratings now  have gone up six points in two weeks  look I always think it's a great thing  for the president to speak directly to  the American people he does that in a  variety of different ways some some days  it's by Twitter some days it's by Town  Hall at the Lincoln Memorial and some  days it's in the press briefing room I  think the important thing is that the  president has been accessible and he has  been very upfront and vote  and shown that he's an actual leader in  this country's time of crisis he stepped  up at a time when we needed him most and  he's been up front and center and I  think that's been really important and  when he needs other people to come in  whether it's the vice president Larry  Kudlow  dr. Fauci and dr. Burks and others to  come forward and talk about a different  message he's done that I think he's done  the right thing in providing constant  and frequent information I love the  different formats and venues I think he  should continue to do that and I also  think Kaylee mackaninee did a phenomenal  job last week in her first press  briefing I think it's a good idea to mix  that up and have her continue to engage  and speak on his behalf as well so Sarah  the New York Times had a brilliant idea  they thought it would be a great idea  for the DNC to investigate Joe Biden  about that sexual assault what could  possibly go wrong let's really get to  the bottom of it because you know  they're gonna drill down deep until they  get that answer so everybody was saying  are you kidding me I think I'm going to  I'm going to reject my subscription  again so also add to this on the  allegation from Tara Reid Fox News has  learned that Ronan Farrow is doing the  extensive piece in The New Yorker on  this listen the last thing this country  needs is any another another sex scandal  to go through it but it's not our choice  where do you think this is heading look  when you first said the New York Times  had a good idea I knew something must be  wrong the idea that the DNC would be the  one to take the lead on any  investigation involving one of their own  candidates is laughable I thought it was  an onion headline not in New York Times  headline they should be embarrassed for  themselves for even suggesting that idea  at the end of the day I think people  just want fairness the hypocrisy that  we've seen from the left is truly  mind-blowing the fact that they went so  aggressively after justice Cavanaugh and  demanded to get to the bottom of things  but want to just brush this aside I  think is the real challenge that most  people are dealing with  now and they want to see a level of  fairness from both sides and the  hypocrisy from the media and the left on  this is is really hard to swallow I  think that we should move forward put  the information out there let the  investigation go where it may and again  maybe joke comes out great and good for  him if he does but at the end of the day  we have to go through the process of the  investigation and see what happens and  it should be fair on both sides okay  Sara thank you for joining us great  thank you so much you're welcome

